flat before and after, the old partners go to ~zero activity afterwards while the new partners were nearly absent beforehand, and the graph's dominant hub (496) belongs to neither cohort, so volume, popularity and time-ignored connectivity cannot explain the pattern."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Change point localization.** The group's activity is steady (~120 events per 3000-unit bin) except for a dip around t\u224812246\u201318246 (step_03), and a complete silence gap in [14246, 16246] (step_16) \u2014 a natural transition boundary.\n\n**Contact sets before vs. after (half-window 5000 around t\u224815246):**\n\n| Node | Before (10246\u201315246) | After (15246\u201320246) | Overlap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 323 | 118, 441, 794 | 337,425,585,977,1147,1181,1247,1387,1725,1734,1847 | 0 |\n| 477 | 118,139,441,788,794,1444,1840 | 306,337,425,585,955,977,1008,1498,1612,1725,1734,1847 | 0 |\n| 865 | 68,118,139,414,441,722,788,794,1057,1145,1444,1702 | 306,337,585,977,1008,1181,1387,1847 | 0 |\n| 1119 | 55,139,441,788,794,901,1009,1057,1145,1444,1702,1836,1840 | 39,337,425,585,1008,1247,1387,1635,1725,1734,1847 | 0 |\n| 1776 | 55,61,68,118,139,441,788,901,1444,1464,1702,1840 | 39,306,425,585,1008,1147,1181,1247 | 0 |\n| 1039 | 118,441,722,788,794,901,1009,1444,1702 | 306,337,425,955,977,1387,1734 | 0 |\n| 1553 | 55,118,139,220,441,722,788,794,901,1057,1702,1840 | 306,337,955,977,1147,1181,1387,1725,1734,1847 | 0 |\n| 1432 | 55,68,441,722,788,1009,1057,1145,1702,1840 | 39,306,337,425,585,955,977,1008,1139,1147,1247 | 0 |\n\nJaccard overlap = **0** for every member tested, and the *same* old cohort {55,68,118,139,441,722,788,794,901,1009,1057,1145,1444,1702,1840} is replaced by the *same* new cohort {39,306,337,425,585,955,977,1008,1147,1181,1247,1387,1725,1734,1847} \u2014 a coordinated, group-wide switch, not independent drift.\n\n**Confounder controls.**\n- *Gradual turnover*: steps 04\u201309 and 10\u201315 show the old set persists essentially unchanged across the three pre-windows (Jaccard \u2248 0.6\u20130.8 between adjacent early windows) and the new set persists unchanged across the three post-windows; all the change is concentrated in one transition, not spread out.\n- *Volume*: total group activity is flat before and after (step_03), so this is not an activity burst/decay artifact.\n- *Popularity*: the old partners are near-dead after the switch (step_29: 55, 139, 722, 1145, 1702, 1840 all have 0 events in 15246\u201330246), and the new partners were near-absent before it (step_30: 425, 1181, 1387 have 0 events in 246\u201314500). So the new contacts are not simply globally-popular hubs, nor is the old set merely globally decaying \u2014 the switch is specific and reciprocal.\n- *Hub artifact*: the graph's one true hub (node 496, 1025 events, step_31) is not in either cohort.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_c1b49572\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [323, 477, 865, 889, 1039, 1119, 1389, 1432, 1530, 1553, 1639, 1776],\n  \"window\": [10246, 20246],\n  \"confidence\": 0.92,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_20\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_23\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_24\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_25\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_26\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_2